Продолжи проектирование LiveSpec vNext, но не начинай реализацию.

Работай read-only. Не редактируй репозиторий, не создавай worktree, не запускай full suite, не коммить и не пушь. Ответ в чате дай по-русски. Все предлагаемые канонические документы, схемы, названия полей и нормативные формулировки должны быть на английском независимо от языка чата.

Возьми как вход:

1. Твой последний архитектурный вердикт о четырёх слоях, parity, shadow mode и vertical slice.
2. Внешний мастер-план:
   /Users/sashaabramovich/live-spec-codex/work/live-spec-vnext-master-roadmap.md
3. Существующие канонические документы LiveSpec — только адресно, через read-only workers. Не загружай их целиком в основную сессию.

Нужно подготовить исправленную архитектурную поправку, закрывающую следующие пробелы.

1. Full parity inventory

Не ограничивайся “representative rows”. Для каждой продуктовой возможности и каждого operational mechanism укажи:

- canonical source;
- specified;
- implemented;
- tested;
- installed;
- actually exercised;
- vNext owner;
- migration proof;
- fate: retain / consolidate / replace / defer / retire;
- fallback.

Не считай наличие текста доказательством реализации.

2. Documentation information architecture

Отдельно спроектируй документную архитектуру для:

- PRODUCT_SPEC.md;
- ARCHITECTURE.md;
- TEST_MATRIX.md;
- ROADMAP.md;
- DECISIONS.md;
- SURFACES.md;
- PROBLEMS.md;
- PROGRESS.md;
- OVERVIEW/README;
- skills and pipeline references.

Для каждого документа укажи:

- audience;
- purpose;
- canonical content;
- content that must not live there;
- duplicated material to remove or replace with links;
- what is always loaded;
- what is loaded on demand;
- readability budget or decomposition rule.

Readability is a product requirement, not cosmetic cleanup. Preserve scenarios, rationale, examples, exceptions and traceability, but organize them through progressive disclosure instead of one giant always-loaded body.

3. Human-facing work graph

Do not assume that ROADMAP notes alone are sufficient.

Reconcile the design with the existing work-board/product requirements, including Requirement 309 and related architecture/roadmap/decisions. Define how every meaningful chat message:

- attaches to an existing card or creates a new one;
- is classified as question, idea, feature, bug, decision, debt or local change;
- preserves provenance;
- exposes stage, owner, dependencies, pipeline, worktree, agents and evidence;
- records updates and history without making normal chat noisy;
- supports parallel and serial work;
- remains readable to a non-technical owner.

Do not invent a competing cards.yaml or second source of truth. First determine which existing canonical surface

content:
Add two mandatory corrections to the design before producing the final verdict.

A. Legacy-host migration is a first-class product route

The existing MIGRATION.md, adoption flow and Requirements 180–182 are inputs, not sufficient proof.

Add R0.5: Legacy-host census and migration contract.

The contract must cover:

- owner-authorized discovery of already adopted LiveSpec projects;
- detected pack version and legacy state shape;
- projects with missing, stale or corrupt `.live-spec` metadata;
- old→new field mapping for canonical documents, queue/work graph, decisions, provenance, profiles, onboarding answers, hooks, gate configuration, installed skills, external-skill pins and local operational state;
- dry run and human-readable change report;
- owner approval;
- checkpoint and non-destructive rollback;
- interruption, resume and idempotence;
- compatibility window and supported legacy versions;
- coexistence rules for legacy and vNext sessions during shadow mode;
- one-writer ownership during cutover;
- shared-machine state migrated once and host projects migrated independently;
- mixed-version projects on one machine;
- privacy and redaction of chat-derived history;
- verification and safe failure back to unchanged legacy LiveSpec.

Require executable or machine-verifiable migration proofs, not only literal-text tests. Include historical fixture hosts and 2–3 representative real projects: oldest available state, paired/multi-repository project and customized-profile project.

B. Documentation system and skill extraction

The existing text-audit skill already owns canonical-English policy, mechanical readability checks and cold-reader comprehension. It does not own cross-document information architecture.

Add R1.5: Documentation architecture and readability contract.

For every canonical document define audience, purpose, owned facts, forbidden content, load tier, links, archive rule and migration rule. Include cross-document contradiction and duplication checks, progressive disclosure and the golden journey “non-English chat produces readable canonical English documents”.

Split skill modularization into:

1. early logical decoupling: stable trigger, inputs, outputs, dependencies, owner, fallback and proof for every skill; route-driven on-demand loading;
2. later physical extraction: external repository/public edition only after the adapter contract is proven.

Proposed extraction order:
product-prover already done;
text-audit as portable document-quality core plus optional LiveSpec adapter;
then independent review/audit skills;
communication/feedback after profile contracts;
spec-author, test-author and build-pipeline only after route contracts stabilize.

Do not physically extract skills merely to reduce repository bytes. A skill may move only when bare-checkout, install, update, offline, compatibility and rollback tests exist.

Also add explicit requirements for:

- versioned work-graph schema and stable task IDs;
- privacy/retention for chat-derived cards;
- external-skill revision pinning and last-known-good fallback;
- portability and clean-host testing;
- dynamic capacity across multiple projects;
- evidence states: specified, implemented, tested, installed, invoked and currently proven.

Reflect these corrections in the final ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH CORRECTIONS / REJECT verdict. Make no repository changes.
